## **4. KV Cache**

**Vanilla Transformer:**

* During inference, recomputes KV for **all past tokens** each step.

**Modern LLMs:**

* Store past **K, V tensors** (KV cache).
* New queries attend only to cached KV + new KV.
* Makes autoregressive decoding **O(1) per token** instead of **O(T)**.

**Math:**

$$
K_{t} = [K_{1}, K_{2}, \dots, K_{t-1}, K_{new}]
$$

**Code:**

```python
# KV cache update
K_cache.append(K_new)
V_cache.append(V_new)
out = attention(Q_new, K_cache, V_cache)
```

