## **7. RoPE Positional Embedding (Rotary)**

**Vanilla:**

* Learned or sinusoidal position embeddings **added** to input.

**Modern (RoPE in LLaMA, GPT-J):**

* Encodes positions via **rotating Q,K vectors in complex space**.
* Handles long-context better, extrapolates.

**Math:**
For position $p$, embedding dim $2i$:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}q_{2i} \\ q_{2i+1}\end{bmatrix}
\mapsto
\begin{bmatrix}
q_{2i} \cos \theta_p - q_{2i+1} \sin \theta_p \\
q_{2i} \sin \theta_p + q_{2i+1} \cos \theta_p
\end{bmatrix}
$$

**Code:**

```python
def apply_rope(q, pos):
    cos, sin = rope_table[pos]
    q_even, q_odd = q[::2], q[1::2]
    q_rot = q_even * cos - q_odd * sin
    q_rot2 = q_even * sin + q_odd * cos
    return torch.stack([q_rot, q_rot2], dim=-1).flatten(-2)
```

