## **8. Multi-Head Latent Attention (MHA → MLA)**

**Vanilla:**

* Attention is directly **token-to-token**.

**Modern (DeepSeek MLA, 2024):**

* Insert latent space → Q maps tokens → latent → attends → back to tokens.
* Reduces cost from O(T²) to O(TL) (L = latent size).

**Math:**

$$
\text{Attention}(X) = \text{softmax}\left(\frac{QX^T}{\sqrt{d}}\right)X
$$

$$
\text{MLA}(X) = \text{softmax}\left(\frac{QW_L}{\sqrt{d}}\right)(W_L^T X)
$$

**Code:**

```python
# Multi-head latent attention
Q_latent = x @ Wq
Latent = torch.randn(batch, latent_dim)
attn_scores = Q_latent @ Latent.T
```

