## **9. Flash Attention**

**Vanilla:**

* Attention = $\text{softmax}(QK^T / \sqrt{d})V$.
* Explicitly materializes attention matrix (O(T²) memory).

**Modern:**

* **FlashAttention** = IO-aware, computes attention in blocks.
* Never stores full attention matrix → linear memory.

**Math:**
Instead of computing full softmax:

$$
\text{softmax}(QK^T)V = \bigoplus_{blocks} \text{softmax\_block}(Q_b, K_b, V_b)
$$

**Code:**

```python
# PyTorch flash attention (xFormers)
out = flash_attn_func(Q, K, V)  # memory-efficient
```

